  "title": "Autopoiesis needs adaptivity for sense-making",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "5aa3d11b-c829-4f63-a8f1-b083d6fc9b12",
      "text": "Mere autopoiesis gives only the all-or-nothing norm of self-continuance, not the graded norms of health, sickness, stress and fatigue that sense-making implies. Autopoiesis and adaptivity are jointly sufficient for sense-making, and mere autopoiesis is insufficient.",
